ZCU208 DDS -> DAC -> ADC -> System ILA : JTAG MODE, VITIS + VIVADO ONLY
(Xilinx example design "DDS Compiler for DAC and System ILA for ADC Capture")
=====================================================================================

Final working folder (everything in one place):

  ~/zcu208_dds_ila/
      design_1_wrapper.bit   <- bitstream            (Vivado impl_1)
      design_1_wrapper.ltx   <- ILA probes file      (Vivado impl_1, same run as .bit)
      fsbl.elf               <- FSBL                 (Vitis platform)
      RFSOC.elf              <- application          (Vitis app)
      boot.tcl               <- xsdb script: loads .bit + FSBL + app over JTAG
      ila.tcl                <- Vivado script: attaches to ILA and captures

Order: Step 1 (folder) -> Step 2 (board) -> Step 3 (Vitis/xsdb) -> Step 4 (Vivado)


=====================================================================================
STEP 1 - CREATE THE FOLDER AND COPY THE FILES
=====================================================================================
Copy-paste into a Linux terminal. Edit the 4 variables first.

------------------------------- copy from here -------------------------------------
VV=/path/to/vv                  # Vivado project folder (the one containing vv.xpr)
WS=/path/to/vitis_workspace     # Vitis workspace folder
PLAT=design_1_wrapper           # your Vitis platform component name
APP=RFSOC                       # your Vitis application component name

mkdir -p ~/zcu208_dds_ila
cd ~/zcu208_dds_ila

cp $VV/vv.runs/impl_1/design_1_wrapper.bit .
cp $VV/vv.runs/impl_1/design_1_wrapper.ltx .
cp $WS/$PLAT/export/$PLAT/sw/boot/fsbl.elf .
cp $WS/$APP/build/$APP.elf ./RFSOC.elf

ls -l
------------------------------- copy to here ---------------------------------------

If a cp fails, locate the file and copy it manually:
  find $VV -name "design_1_wrapper.bit" -o -name "*.ltx"
  find $WS -name "fsbl*.elf"
  find $WS -name "$APP.elf"

Then create the two scripts (copy-paste each block as-is, still inside ~/zcu208_dds_ila):

------------------------------- boot.tcl : copy from here --------------------------
cat > ~/zcu208_dds_ila/boot.tcl <<'EOF'
# boot.tcl - JTAG boot: reset -> program PL -> FSBL -> app  (slide 37 sequence)
set here [file dirname [file normalize [info script]]]
set bit  $here/design_1_wrapper.bit
set fsbl $here/fsbl.elf
set app  $here/RFSOC.elf

connect
targets -set -nocase -filter {name =~ "*PSU*"}
rst -system
after 3000

puts "Programming PL ..."
fpga -file $bit

puts "Running FSBL ..."
targets -set -nocase -filter {name =~ "*A53*#0"}
rst -processor -clear-registers
dow $fsbl
set bp [bpadd -addr &XFsbl_Exit]
con -block -timeout 60
bpremove $bp

puts "Running application ..."
targets -set -nocase -filter {name =~ "*A53*#0"}
rst -processor
dow $app
con
puts "Done - application is running"
disconnect
EOF
------------------------------- boot.tcl : copy to here ----------------------------

------------------------------- ila.tcl : copy from here ---------------------------
cat > ~/zcu208_dds_ila/ila.tcl <<'EOF'
# ila.tcl - attach Vivado to the running design and capture the System ILA
# NOTE: does NOT program the device (that would reset the RF data converter)
set here [file dirname [file normalize [info script]]]
set ltx  $here/design_1_wrapper.ltx

open_hw_manager
connect_hw_server -url localhost:3121
open_hw_target
set dev [get_hw_devices xczu48dr_0]
current_hw_device $dev
set_property PROBES.FILE      $ltx $dev
set_property FULL_PROBES.FILE $ltx $dev
refresh_hw_device $dev

set ila [get_hw_ilas hw_ila_1]
run_hw_ila -trigger_now $ila
wait_on_hw_ila $ila
display_hw_ila_data [upload_hw_ila_data $ila]
puts "ILA capture done"
EOF
------------------------------- ila.tcl : copy to here -----------------------------

Check the folder now has all 6 files:
  ls -l ~/zcu208_dds_ila


=====================================================================================
STEP 2 - BOARD (slide 9)
=====================================================================================
  - Coax: DAC Tile228 Ch0 -> ADC Tile226 Ch0 on XM655 (low-frequency balun SMAs)
  - USB cable to PC
  - SW2 = on, on, on, on   (JTAG boot)
  - Power ON


=====================================================================================
STEP 3 - VITIS: BOOT OVER JTAG (run boot.tcl with xsdb)
=====================================================================================
Use ONE of these two ways - both talk to the same hw_server, result is identical.

  (a) Normal Linux terminal:
        source <XILINX_INSTALL>/Vitis/<version>/settings64.sh
        cd ~/zcu208_dds_ila
        xsdb boot.tcl

  (b) Inside the Vitis IDE: open the XSDB console (Vitis menu -> XSDB Console),
      then type:
        cd ~/zcu208_dds_ila
        source boot.tcl

  Expected end of output:  "Done - application is running"

  Optional - app log (slide 39) in the Vitis IDE serial terminal, 115200 baud:
       DAC Tile0 Power-on Sequence Step: 0x0000000F
       ADC Tile2 Power-on Sequence Step: 0x0000000F
       ------------- Startup Complete -------------


=====================================================================================
STEP 4 - VIVADO: VIEW THE ILA (run ila.tcl)
=====================================================================================
  source <XILINX_INSTALL>/Vivado/<version>/settings64.sh
  cd ~/zcu208_dds_ila
  vivado -source ila.tcl &

  Vivado GUI opens, connects, loads the probes and shows the captured waveform.

  !! Never click "Program Device" / run program_hw_devices.
     The PL is already programmed by boot.tcl. If it happens: rerun step 3, then step 4.

  Display (slides 44-46), for both slot_0 TDATA and slot_1 TDATA:
    Right-click -> Waveform Style -> Analog
    Right-click -> Waveform Style -> Analog Settings -> Row height 100
    Right-click -> Radix -> Signed Decimal

  New capture: press >> in the waveform toolbar, or in the Tcl Console:
    run_hw_ila -trigger_now [get_hw_ilas hw_ila_1]
    wait_on_hw_ila [get_hw_ilas hw_ila_1]
    display_hw_ila_data [upload_hw_ila_data [get_hw_ilas hw_ila_1]]


=====================================================================================
STEP 5 - PASS CHECK
=====================================================================================
  [ ] TVALID = 1 on both slots (TREADY = 1 on slot_1)
  [ ] slot_0 (DDS -> DAC) : clean sine
  [ ] slot_1 (ADC)        : clean sine, same frequency, smaller amplitude, not clipped
  [ ] Period ~18.4 samples (10 MHz at 184.32 MSPS) -> 5 cycles ~92 samples
  [ ] Unplug coax -> slot_1 drops to noise, slot_0 unchanged


=====================================================================================
IF SOMETHING FAILS
=====================================================================================
  cp: cannot stat ...               -> use the find commands in step 1
  xsdb: no targets                  -> SW2 not on,on,on,on or USB cable issue
  "con -block" times out            -> fsbl.elf not from this XSA; power-cycle, redo step 3
  Vivado: no hw_ila_1 / no clock    -> app not running; redo step 3, then step 4
  slot_1 flat                       -> coax on wrong SMA or on the HF balun
  after power cycle                 -> redo steps 3 and 4 (JTAG mode keeps nothing on board)
